      Silicon designers scale vector acceleration along a well-defined progression: from area-minimized single-lane microcontroller coprocessors up through multi-lane monolithic RVV units, clustered scale-up fabrics, 2D systolic meshes, and full-stack SIMT GPGPUs.
    </p>

