        <h3 class="dossier-title">Ara &bull; Scalable 4&ndash;16 Lane Monolithic RVV 1.0 Coprocessor</h3>
        <span class="dossier-sub">ETH Zurich &amp; University of Bologna &bull; Apache-2.0 &bull; SystemVerilog</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Specs Stack -->
      <div class="dossier-specs-grid">
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">ISA:</span><span class="s-v"><code>RV64GCV (Vector 1.0 Compliant)</code></span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Lanes:</span><span class="s-v">4 to 16 Parallel SIMD Lanes</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Vector Length:</span><span class="s-v">512 to 4096 bits (VLEN)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">VRF Architecture:</span><span class="s-v">8 SRAM Banks per Lane &bull; Monolithic Crossbar</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Host / Bus Interface:</span><span class="s-v">128-bit to 512-bit AXI4 Crossbar</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Silicon Footprint:</span><span class="s-v"><strong>~220 kGE (4 Lanes) / ~850 kGE (16 Lanes)</strong></span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Peak Frequency:</span><span class="s-v">1.05 GHz @ 0.8V (GF 22FDX)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Verification Status:</span><span class="s-v">SCORE Cycle-Accurate Verilator &amp; Spike Co-Sim</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="dossier-body">
        <p>Ara is a scalable, open-source vector coprocessor co-designed to accelerate high-performance scientific and machine learning workloads when coupled to the CVA6 64-bit application core. It features full compliance with the ratified RISC-V Vector Extension version 1.0. Ara's vector execution unit is physically partitioned into independent parallel lanes, each containing a dedicated integer ALU, a multi-precision floating-point unit (FP64/FP32/FP16), and eight single-port SRAM banks to prevent read conflicts during chained vector arithmetic.</p>

        <!-- RTL Configuration Parameters Table -->
        <h4 style="font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #151b20;">&bull; Key RTL Configuration Parameters</h4>
        <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <table class="data-table" style="font-size: 0.8rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default</th><th>Silicon Impact</th><th>Description</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>NrLanes</code></td><td><code>4</code></td><td>Datapath Area &times; N</td><td>Number of parallel SIMD execution lanes (1, 2, 4, 8, or 16).</td></tr><tr><td><code>VLEN</code></td><td><code>4096</code></td><td>VRF Storage Size</td><td>Vector register file width in bits. Sets maximum elements per vector register.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ELEN</code></td><td><code>64</code></td><td>Datapath Element Width</td><td>Maximum element width supported (64-bit for standard double precision).</td></tr><tr><td><code>NumBanks</code></td><td><code>8</code></td><td>Crossbar Decoders</td><td>Number of independent single-port SRAM banks instantiated per lane.</td></tr><tr><td><code>AxiDataWidth</code></td><td><code>128</code></td><td>Memory Bandwidth</td><td>Data bus width connecting Vector Load-Store Unit to system L2 cache.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <!-- Microarchitectural Deep-Dive -->
        <div class="dossier-deep-dive" style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 3px solid #3b82f6; padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;">
          <h4 style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 900; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Microarchitectural Deep-Dive:</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #334155; margin: 0;">Ara implements element-wise vector chaining through fine-grained hazard scoreboards. A dependent vector instruction (e.g. <code>vadd.vv</code>) begins executing as soon as the first element slice of its source operand retires from the FPU pipeline, without waiting for the full 4096-bit register to finish. Each lane features an internal crossbar routing operands between the 8 local SRAM banks and the FPU, ALU, and Permute units.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Verified Benchmarks Table -->
        <h4 style="font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #151b20;">&bull; Cycle-Accurate Verified Benchmark Results</h4>
        <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <table class="data-table" style="font-size: 0.8rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Workload</th><th>Type</th><th>Cycles</th><th>Ops / Cycle</th><th>Utilization %</th><th>Evidence Source</th></tr>
