        <!-- Microarchitectural Deep-Dive -->
        <div class="dossier-deep-dive" style="background: #f8fafc; border-left: 3px solid #3b82f6; padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;">
          <h4 style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 900; color: #1e3a8a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">Microarchitectural Deep-Dive:</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #334155; margin: 0;">Vicuna utilizes a dedicated 128-bit memory interface to burst full 16-element INT8 vectors in a single cycle. Its microcoded sequencer folds vector loop iterations over a 32-bit ALU and multiplier, achieving 80.7% utilization on INT8 GEMM with a footprint under 50 kGE.</p>
        </div>

