      <div class="dossier-body">
        <p>Hwacha is a decoupled vector-fetch coprocessor developed at UC Berkeley. Using the Vector-Thread (VT) execution model, Hwacha decouples vector instruction fetch and address generation from arithmetic execution. Decoupled queues buffer operands between memory and compute units, allowing Hwacha to tolerate extreme memory latencies without execution lane stalls.</p>

        <!-- RTL Configuration Parameters Table -->
        <h4 style="font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: #151b20;">&bull; Key RTL Configuration Parameters</h4>
